---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Mitchell Haw | SEO, AI Search & Digital Strategy"
  description="Mitchell Haw helps brands improve visibility across Google, AI search, maps, content, local discovery, and the changing search landscape."
  image="/images/mitchell-haw.jpg"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@graph": [
        {
          "@type": "Person",
          "@id": "https://mitchellhaw.com/#person",
          "name": "Mitchell Haw",
          "url": "https://mitchellhaw.com/",
          "jobTitle": "Digital Strategist & SEO / AI Search Lead",
          "image": "https://mitchellhaw.com/images/mitchell-haw.jpg",
          "sameAs": [
            "https://www.linkedin.com/in/mitchellhaw"
          ],
          "description": "Digital strategist specializing in SEO, AI search, local visibility, content strategy, and organic growth."
        },
        {
          "@type": "WebSite",
          "@id": "https://mitchellhaw.com/#website",
          "url": "https://mitchellhaw.com/",
          "name": "Mitchell Haw",
          "publisher": {
            "@id": "https://mitchellhaw.com/#person"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  </script>

  <main class="home-main">
    <section class="home-hero">
      <div class="container home-hero-inner">
        <div>
          <p class="home-kicker">Mitchell Haw / Search Strategy</p>
          <h1>
            Search is changing.<br />
            I help brands stay <em>visible.</em>
          </h1>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="home-hero-bottom">
            <p class="home-hero-copy">
              SEO, AI search, local discovery, content, analytics, and digital strategy for a world where people no longer search in just one place.
            </p>

            <div class="home-hero-actions">
              <a class="home-link-primary" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a>
              <a class="home-link-secondary" href="#work">See what I do</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="home-meta" aria-label="Areas of focus">
            <span>SEO</span>
            <span>AI Search</span>
            <span>Content Strategy</span>
            <span>Bend, Oregon</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-shift">
      <div class="container home-shift-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="home-section-kicker">The shift</p>
          <h2>People don't search in <em>one place</em> anymore.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="home-shift-copy">
          <p>
            Search now moves between traditional results, AI answers, maps, video, reviews, communities, and recommendations. The job is not simply to rank. It is to make a brand useful, understandable, and discoverable across the whole journey.
          </p>

          <div class="channel-words" aria-label="Search and discovery channels">
            <span>Google</span>
            <span>ChatGPT</span>
            <span>Maps</span>
            <span>YouTube</span>
            <span>Reviews</span>
            <span>Reddit</span>
            <span>AI Answers</span>
            <span>Content</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-services" id="work">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="home-section-head">
          <p class="home-section-kicker">What I do</p>
          <h2>Strategy for how people find things now.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="service-rows">
          <article class="service-row">
            <span class="row-number">01</span>
            <h3>SEO Strategy</h3>
            <p>
              Technical SEO, site architecture, migrations, internal linking, search intent, content planning, and organic growth strategy.
            </p>
            <a class="row-link" href="/services/seo/" aria-label="Explore SEO strategy">Explore</a>
          </article>

          <article class="service-row">
            <span class="row-number">02</span>
            <h3>AI Search</h3>
            <p>
              Understand and improve how a brand appears across ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity, AI Overviews, and the answer engines changing discovery.
            </p>
            <a class="row-link" href="/services/ai-search/" aria-label="Explore AI search strategy">Explore</a>
          </article>

          <article class="service-row">
            <span class="row-number">03</span>
            <h3>Local Discovery</h3>
            <p>
              Google Maps, Business Profile strategy, reviews, local landing pages, listings, and the signals that help businesses win nearby searches.
            </p>
            <a class="row-link" href="/services/seo-bend-oregon/" aria-label="Explore local SEO">Explore</a>
          </article>

          <article class="service-row">
            <span class="row-number">04</span>
            <h3>Content & Video</h3>
            <p>
              Useful content systems built around real questions, search behavior, video discovery, and the information people actually need.
            </p>
            <a class="row-link" href="/services/video-marketing/" aria-label="Explore video and content strategy">Explore</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-work">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="home-section-head">
          <p class="home-section-kicker">Selected focus</p>
          <h2>Less marketing theater. More useful work.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="work-rows">
          <article class="work-row">
            <span class="row-number">01</span>
            <div>
              <span class="row-type">Enterprise search</span>
              <h3>Large websites & migrations</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              Search strategy across complex, multi-location websites: architecture, technical foundations, migrations, content systems, measurement, and organic visibility.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="work-row">
            <span class="row-number">02</span>
            <div>
              <span class="row-type">Local discovery</span>
              <h3>Central Oregon businesses</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              Practical local search work across websites, Google Maps, content, reviews, and location signals—with a close-up view from Bend, Oregon.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="work-row">
            <span class="row-number">03</span>
            <div>
              <span class="row-type">Emerging search</span>
              <h3>AI visibility & measurement</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              Testing how brands surface in AI answers, what those systems retrieve and cite, and how search strategy changes when discovery becomes conversational.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-about">
      <div class="container home-about-grid">
        <div class="home-about-media">
          <img
            src="/images/mitchell-haw.jpg"
            alt="Mitchell Haw, digital strategist based in Bend, Oregon"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="home-about-copy">
          <div>
            <p class="home-section-kicker">About</p>
            <h2>I'm Mitchell. I work where search, content, data, and <em>curiosity</em> overlap.</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="home-about-body">
            <p>
              I’m a digital strategist focused on SEO, AI search, content strategy, local visibility, analytics, and organic growth.
            </p>
            <p>
              My work spans large national websites, local businesses, and my own web projects. I like technical problems, useful content, clear measurement, and figuring out what changed before turning it into a slide full of jargon.
            </p>
            <p>
              I’m based in Bend, Oregon, and I’m especially interested in where search is headed next—not just where it has been.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/about/">More about me</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-notes">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="home-section-head">
          <p class="home-section-kicker">How I think</p>
          <h2>A few things I believe about modern search.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="note-rows">
          <article class="note-row">
            <span class="row-number">01</span>
            <h3>SEO is not dead. The surface area got bigger.</h3>
            <p>
              Traditional search still matters. So do AI answers, maps, video, reviews, communities, and the sources those systems use to form an answer.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="note-row">
            <span class="row-number">02</span>
            <h3>Useful beats optimized-looking.</h3>
            <p>
              The best content answers something clearly, earns trust, and gives people a reason to stay. Search optimization should make that easier—not bury it.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="note-row">
            <span class="row-number">03</span>
            <h3>Measurement needs to evolve with discovery.</h3>
            <p>
              Rankings and traffic are only part of the picture now. Visibility, citations, brand persistence, local discovery, and assisted journeys matter too.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-final">
      <div class="container home-final-inner">
        <p class="home-section-kicker">Let's talk</p>
        <h2>Have a search problem worth <em>figuring out?</em></h2>
        <div class="home-final-line">
          <p>
            Whether it is a migration, an AI-search question, a local visibility problem, or a bigger organic strategy challenge, I’m always interested in the problem first.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
